prompt:
Create unit `tasks` and implement `deposit_all`: for a ledger `a` (every balance in [0, 1000000000], as `ledger::amount_ok` states) and an amount x in [0, 1000000000], deposit x into every account that has room for it and return how many deposits succeeded. The contract must state that all balances stay in [0, 1000000000] and that the result is at most a.len(). Reuse the existing library (see `query units`) where it helps.

Required signature (in unit `tasks`):
fn deposit_all(a: &mut [i64], x: i64) -> (r: usize)

reference.code:
spec fn count_ok(a: &[i64], r: usize) -> bool { r <= a.len() }

#[effects(pure)]
#[uses(ledger::amount_ok, ledger::debited, ledger::in_closed, count_ok)]
fn deposit_all(a: &mut [i64], x: i64) -> (r: usize)
    requires ledger::amount_ok(a), ledger::in_closed(x),
    ensures ledger::amount_ok(a), count_ok(a, r),
{
    let mut c: usize = 0;
    let mut k: usize = 0;
    while k < a.len()
        invariant k <= a.len(), c <= k, ledger::amount_ok(a),
        decreases a.len() - k,
    {
        if ledger::count_state(a, k, x) {
            c = c + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    c
}

